            "description": "Watch Pittsburgh Riverhounds vs Indy Eleven highlights and goals from USL Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 13, 2026. On the evening of June 13, 2026 , the USL Championship spotlight turned to the clash between Pittsburgh Riverhounds and Indy Eleven . Both teams entered the pitch with high expectations, setting the stage for a gritty tactical encounter. A Battle for Control The match began with high intensity as both sides looked to establish dominance in the midfield. Throughout the first hour of play, clear-cut chances were hard to come by, with both defensive units maintaining a disciplined shape. The atmosphere grew increasingly tense as the second half progressed, with physical challenges becoming more frequent as the players fought for every inch of grass. Discipline became a talking point midway through the second half. Indy Eleven 's P. Craig was the first to enter the referee's book in the 56th minute, followed shortly by O. Mikoy of the Pittsburgh Riverhounds in the 62nd minute. These cautions reflected the competitive nature of the fixture, as neither side was willing to give the other a clear path to goal. Stoppage Time Drama Just as it looked like the points would be shared in a scoreless draw, the game reached a fever pitch in stoppage time. In the 92nd minute, the breakthrough finally arrived for the home supporters. P. Barnes delivered a crucial assist to L. Kelp , who kept his composure to slot the ball home and give the Pittsburgh Riverhounds a dramatic 1-0 lead. Indy Eleven attempted a late surge to salvage a result, but the closing moments were defined by further cautions. L. Neidlinger received a yellow card for the visitors in the 95th minute, while A. Dikwa was also booked for the hosts in the 96th minute as they looked to see out the game. Ultimately, the late heroics from Kelp were enough to secure all three points for Pittsburgh in a memorable finish."
